# The build context is the whole monorepo, so what is excluded here is the
# difference between a fast build and shipping a 2GB tarball to the daemon.

# Installed inside the image by `npm ci` — a host node_modules is both huge and
# wrong, because it may hold darwin-arm64 binaries for a linux/amd64 image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. `.next` in particular must not be copied in: a stale local
# build would be overwritten by the builder stage, but only after being sent
# over the wire.
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. `.env` holds a local DATABASE_URL and would otherwise be baked into
# the image, where it would also *win* over the environment ECS injects —
# `loadRootEnv` uses `override: false`, so a file that should not be there
# would not be overridden, it would be preferred.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
infra/terraform

# Documentation and local tooling: nothing the build reads.
*.md
!README.md
docs
.claude
.cursor
.rocketride
.mcp.json.example
